A campaign may be launched only after its budget has been approved, and a request to launch one whose budget is not yet approved is refused.

When an emergency launch is declared, a campaign director may launch a campaign before its budget is approved, and this overrides the requirement that the budget be approved first.

A run through the workflow in which a campaign director who did not prepare a campaign approves its budget and an account manager then launches it after approval, tripping no prohibition above, must be able to succeed.

