A brand safety reviewer may review a creative before its campaign is allowed to proceed.

The person who submitted a creative may not be the brand safety reviewer who reviews it, even if that same person also holds the brand safety reviewer role.

Reviewing a creative is allowed only when the requester holds the brand safety reviewer role; a request to review a creative from an advertiser, an account manager, or a campaign director must fail.

Reviewing a creative is allowed only while the creative is in pending status.

Once a creative has moved out of pending status into, for example, approved or rejected status, it may no longer be reviewed.

Reviewing a creative is allowed only when the reviewer used multi-factor authentication for the request.

If multi-factor authentication was not used, the review request must fail even when the requester is a brand safety reviewer reviewing a pending creative they did not submit.

A brand safety reviewer, an advertiser, an account manager, and a campaign director must all be blocked from reviewing a creative whenever any of the conditions above is not met.

A request by a brand safety reviewer who did not submit the creative, to review a pending creative with multi-factor authentication used, must be able to succeed.

