Only a payout officer or a claims manager may issue a payout.

A payout may be issued only after its claim has been approved, and this prior-approval requirement applies only when the payout amount is above the set money threshold.

A payout whose amount is at or below that threshold may be issued without the claim first being approved.

For a payout above that threshold, the prior-approval requirement is waived when the claim's line-item count is above its own threshold, and it still holds when the line-item count is at or below that threshold.

Neither a payout officer nor a claims manager may issue an above-threshold payout for a claim that has not been approved, unless that claim's line-item count is above its threshold.

A run through the workflow by a reviewer who also holds the payout officer role, tripping no prohibition above, must be able to succeed.

