In this workflow an asset is first calibrated and then its return to service is approved, and the approval step can see the asset's status and the technician who calibrated it as recorded by the calibration step.

A calibration technician or senior technician may perform a calibration only when their certification level is at least the asset's equipment class.

For an asset whose measurement-point count is above the extended-procedure threshold, that certification-level requirement is set aside and the calibration follows the extended procedure instead.

A quality inspector or metrology manager may approve an asset's return to service only after it has reached the calibrated state.

When the approval is submitted from the plant network, this after-calibration requirement is lifted and the return may be approved even before the asset is calibrated.

Off the plant network, a quality inspector or metrology manager may not approve the return to service of an asset that is not yet calibrated.

A run through the workflow in which a calibration technician whose certification level is at least the asset's equipment class calibrates it and a quality inspector on the plant network then approves its return to service, tripping no prohibition above, must be able to succeed.

