A requester who does not belong under the resource's org unit must not modify it, even if they are its owner.

A cloud resource may be modified only when the request comes from an allowed network range.

A request that does not come from an allowed network range must not modify the resource, even from its owner.

A request by the owner of a cloud resource, made from an allowed network range and from within the resource's own org unit, to modify that resource outside of production, must be able to succeed.

