This after-verification requirement is waived when the requester holds the qualifying role, who may release the result even before verification.

This after-verification requirement is also waived when the result's sensitivity is at least the restricted level, reflecting that a restricted result is handled by a pathologist regardless of the verification step.

Before a result is pushed to the patient portal, the releaser's credential level must be high enough to cover the result's sensitivity, and a releaser whose credential level does not cover it may not push it to the portal.

