## Access-Control Requirement
This document sets requirements for zone control in a smart-building automation system.

The people involved are facility managers, zone controllers, maintenance technicians, and tenants. One person may hold both the facility manager and the zone controller role at the same time.

The resources are actuators, zones, and commission requests. Every actuator records its owner, its zone group, its device tags, its maintenance flag, and its status. Every zone records its assigned controller, its criticality level, and its status. Every commission request records the device it targets, who requested it, and its status.

Each requester carries a control tier and a record of which groups they belong to, and each request carries the current time, whether occupancy is detected, whether it originates on the site network, and whether a maintenance override is active.

A zone's schedule may be overridden only when the requester's control tier is at least as high as that zone's criticality level.

A schedule override may be carried out only when the requester holds the zone controller role for that zone; a facility manager who does not also hold the zone controller role for a zone may not override its schedule, while a facility manager who does hold the zone controller role for that zone may override it on the same terms as any other zone controller.

A schedule override may be carried out only when the zone's status is not locked; a zone controller may override the schedule of a zone whose status is active, but not one whose status is locked.

A schedule override may be carried out only when the zone currently has occupancy detected; a zone controller may override the schedule of an occupied zone, but not one where no occupancy is detected.

Neither a zone controller nor a facility manager may override the schedule of a zone that is locked, that has no occupancy detected, or whose criticality level is not dominated by their control tier.

A maintenance technician may request commission of a device, and a facility manager may approve that commission request.

A tenant may view the status of a zone.

A request by a zone controller to override the schedule of an occupied, unlocked zone whose criticality their control tier dominates must be able to succeed.

