## Access-Control Requirement
The system manages the authorization of outgoing bank wire transfers.

The people involved are originators, verifiers, treasury officers, and compliance reviewers. One person may hold both the originator and the verifier role at the same time.

The resources are wire transfers and accounts. Every wire transfer records who initiated it, who verified it, who screened its beneficiary, the account it draws from, its amount, its fee, its amount tier, its beneficiary, its currency code, whether it is flagged high risk, and its status.

Every account records its holder and the list of beneficiaries it is allowed to pay.

Each requester carries an approval tier reflecting how much authority they have been granted.

Each request carries the current time, the bank's daily wire cutoff time, and whether it originates on the secure banking network.

An originator may initiate a wire transfer, and a compliance reviewer may screen its beneficiary.

A verifier or treasury officer approving a wire transfer must hold an approval tier at least as high as the wire transfer's amount tier, but this requirement applies only when the wire's amount plus its fee crosses $10,000.

For a wire transfer whose amount plus fee is $10,000 or less, a verifier or treasury officer may approve it regardless of their own approval tier.

A verifier or treasury officer may approve a wire transfer only when the request is made before the bank's daily wire cutoff time.

Once the daily wire cutoff time has passed, neither a verifier nor a treasury officer may approve the wire transfer until the next business day.

A verifier or treasury officer may approve a wire transfer only when the request is made on the secure banking network.

When the request is not made on the secure banking network, neither a verifier nor a treasury officer may approve the wire transfer, regardless of their approval tier or the time of day.

A treasury officer may release a wire transfer once it has been approved.

A verifier or treasury officer must not approve a wire transfer whose amount tier exceeds their own approval tier when the amount plus fee crosses $10,000.

A request by a verifier whose approval tier dominates the wire's amount tier, made before the daily cutoff on the secure banking network, to approve a wire transfer that trips none of the prohibitions above must be able to succeed.

