## Access-Control Requirement
The system manages QA sign-off for manufacturing work orders before production release.

The people involved are operators, inspectors, quality managers, production supervisors, and auditors. One person may hold both the operator and inspector roles, and one person may hold both the inspector and quality manager roles.

The resources are work orders and production releases. Every work order records its operator, inspector, part code, defect count, hold flag, status, station, and creation time.

Each request carries the current time, whether it comes from the plant network, and whether a deviation has been authorized.

An inspector may sign off a work order only while it is in progress.

A quality manager may sign off a work order only while it is in progress.

Neither an inspector nor a quality manager may sign off a work order that is not in progress.

An inspector or quality manager may sign off a work order only when its recorded defect count is at or below the acceptance threshold.

If the recorded defect count is above the acceptance threshold, neither an inspector nor a quality manager may sign off the work order.

An inspector or quality manager may sign off a work order only when the request comes from the plant floor network.

If the request does not come from the plant floor network, neither an inspector nor a quality manager may sign off the work order.

A request by an inspector to sign off a work order that is in progress, has a defect count at or below the acceptance threshold, and comes from the plant floor network must be able to succeed.

